{"name":"Frenzy","hex":"#feb101","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frenzy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of wild activity or panic.","A violent agitation of the mind approaching madness; rage."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Mad; frantic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frenzy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Frenzy","blocks":[{"text":"Frenzy is a 1972 British neo-noir thriller film directed and produced by Alfred Hitchcock. It is the penultimate feature film of his extensive career. The screenplay by Anthony Shaffer is based on the 1966 novel Goodbye Piccadilly, Farewell Leicester Square by Arthur La Bern. The film stars Jon Finch, Alec McCowen and Barry Foster and features Billie Whitelaw, Anna Massey, Barbara Leigh-Hunt, Bernard Cribbins and Vivien Merchant. The original music score was composed by Ron Goodwin."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/eb/Frenzy_movieposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frenzy"},{"title":"Frenzy (Split Enz album)","blocks":[{"text":"Frenzy is the fourth studio album by the New Zealand new wave band Split Enz. Frenzy ventured further beyond the band's art rock roots to more of a pop sound."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9a/Frenzy-enz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frenzy_(Split_Enz_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Frenzy_Henieretta_Street.JPG/500px-Frenzy_Henieretta_Street.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Frenzy_Henieretta_Street.JPG/1280px-Frenzy_Henieretta_Street.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6